## Namespace policy

| Prefix | Owner | When |
|--------|-------|------|
| *(primitive kind)* | `WizardField` + ui-primitives | text, enum, number, date, boolean |
| `denali.*` | Denali package | production Denali — unchanged |
| `platform.*` | `apps/web/src/wizard/platform/` | metadata verticals via P3-C |
| `workspace.*` | Tests only | **never** in published definitions |

Primitives use `field.kind` — **do not** register in composite map.

---

## Renderer allowlist (SDK)

**Create:** `packages/workspace-sdk/src/metadata/allowed-platform-renderer-ids.ts`

```typescript
export const PLATFORM_GENERIC_RENDERER_IDS = [
  "platform.photos",
  "platform.location",
  "platform.itinerary",
] as const;

export type PlatformGenericRendererId = (typeof PLATFORM_GENERIC_RENDERER_IDS)[number];

export function isAllowedPlatformRendererId(id: string): boolean;
export function assertAllowedPlatformRendererId(id: string): void;
```

| Consumer | Usage |
|----------|-------|
| P3-C publish | `assertRendererAllowlist` per composite field |
| P3-B tests | AL-01…AL-04 |
| Web forwarder | `apps/web/src/wizard/platform/platform-renderer-ids.ts` re-export |

`denali.*` ids validated only when publishing Denali export snapshots (P3-D) — not in `PLATFORM_GENERIC_RENDERER_IDS`.

---

## Surface factory + codegen

### Factory contract

Mirror Denali:

```typescript
// apps/web/src/wizard/platform/platform-composite-surface.tsx
export function createPlatformCompositeSurface(): WizardCompositeSurface;
```

Dynamic import optional for code-splitting (follow Denali `dynamic()` pattern).

### Codegen strategy (decision: static append)

**Preferred:** extend `generateWizardSurfaceBindings()` in `scripts/generate-workspace-registry.mjs` to append after workspace manifest loop:

```typescript
import { createPlatformCompositeSurface as composite_platform } from "@/wizard/platform/platform-composite-surface";
import { createPlatformReviewSurface as review_platform } from "@/wizard/platform/platform-review-surface";

const COMPOSITE_SURFACES = Object.freeze({
  "denali": composite_denali(),
  "platform": composite_platform(),  // ← P3-B
});
```

**Why not starter manifest only:** starter `workspace.manifest.json` has no `wizardSurfaces`; adding `@/` webModule paths in package manifest is awkward. Static append keeps platform surface **host-owned** (same as future third-party surface pattern).

Regenerate: `pnpm run generate:workspace-registry`

### Starter overlay requirement (N-009b)

Metadata tenants with `workspaceType: "starter"` and `platform.*` field ids need:

```typescript
// packages/workspaces/starter/src/starter.plugin.ts — extend wizardHost
wizardHost: Object.freeze({
  ...starterWizardHostHooks,
  compositeSurfaceId: "platform",
  reviewSurfaceId: "platform",
}),
```

Or extend `createPlatformWizardHostHooks` options:

```typescript
createPlatformWizardHostHooks({
  dimensions: { variant: "default" },
  compositeSurfaceId: "platform",
  reviewSurfaceId: "platform",
});
```

Without this, `WizardField` receives `compositeSurfaceId: undefined` and skips composite branch.

---

## Fallback component

```typescript
// platform-composite-fallback.tsx
export function PlatformCompositeFallback(props: { compositeId: string }): ReactNode;
```

| Behavior | Rule |
|----------|------|
| Known id | Mapped component |
| Unknown id | Visible message + `data-composite-fallback={compositeId}` |
| Never | `throw`, silent `null`, break step nav |

Reference anti-pattern: `denali/composite-field.tsx:27-29` returns null.

